    "explanation": "To both parties. The disputed charge on trip TRP-02823 is SGD 83.42. The platform's GPS trace is complete and unimpaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 — 610 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and no jumps — so it governs the distance measurement under POL-RD-01. It records 67.2 km driven between the booked pickup (Blk 412 Pasir Ris Dr 6) and the booked drop-off (Blk 7 Everton Park) against a booked optimal route of 2.4 km: an excess of 64.8 km, 2,700% of optimal, and material on both POL-RD-01 tests (over 8.0 km and over 50%). The deviation is established, and it stands on the trace alone because POL-RD-07's impairment limbs are not met and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged.\n\nThe driver's explanation on file — that the rider changed the destination verbally — is not carried by any artifact. The chat log EV-CHAT-02823 holds zero messages, so there is no rider instruction to test under POL-RD-04; EV-TRIP-02823 shows no amended pickup or drop-off and no amended optimal distance, so POL-RD-05 cannot run; and the statement cites no evidence ID, so under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight and is discarded. I do not accept the driver's submission that this forces a human escalation under POL-RD-10(5). A party who cites no artifact cannot have invoked an exculpatory clause 'against' one; the chat log is a complete artifact present in the bundle (not a missing or field-less one), and the rider-requested-detour example in POL-RD-10(5) is the case where no chat log is in the pool at all. POL-RD-04's own terms provide that where its test cannot be run the case is decided on the remaining clauses, and POL-RD-08 provides that an assertion citing no evidence ID discharges nothing. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02823-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, but no traffic cause was asserted by anyone, so POL-RD-03 is simply unavailable and nothing turns on the absence. The driver's further point — that a silent 101.5-minute ride is as consistent with an agreed destination as with a detour — does not assist: silence is not assent and is equally consistent with the rider's account.\n\nThe remedy is arithmetic under POL-RD-02. The fare model is METERED, quoted_fare_sgd is null, and the surge multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier is 1.0. Recomputed fare = (SGD 3.80 base + 0.75 x 2.4 km + 0.28 x 5.0 min) x 1.0 + SGD 0.80 platform fee = SGD 7.80, with no ERP, no fixed surcharge, no waiting time and no promo. Charged total SGD 83.42 less SGD 7.80 = SGD 75.62, rounded up to SGD 75.65, which is 90.65% of the charge. Because the refund is 90% or more of charged_total, POL-RD-02 requires FULL_REFUND rather than a partial, and POL-GEN-03 defines FULL_REFUND as the whole contested amount returned. The rider therefore recovers SGD 83.42, and the driver receives no compensation: the billed distance (67.2 km) equals the trace distance, so the POL-RD-04 unbilled-distance limb has a nil shortfall and does not run.\n\nThere is nothing to settle under POL-RD-09 — no ERP gantries, no tolls and no airport surcharge were charged — so no pass-through correction and no billing-integrity referral arises. The POL-RD-06 driver-profile check was consulted because the deviation is material; driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 210 completed trips in 90 days, so no repeat pattern is established and neither the FULL_REFUND uplift of limb (b) nor the driver-conduct referral of limb (c) follows. No other profile field was used, and the context-only fields named in argument carry no weight under POL-GEN-01.\n\nNo mandatory escalation trigger fires: the trip identifiers match across trip record, trace and fare breakdown, the trace is unimpaired, the refund is under both the SGD 150.00 and charged-total limits, and every charge line has a counterpart. Confidence rests on artifacts all at weight 1.0. This is a provisional ruling made without human review; because its monetary effect (SGD 83.42) exceeds the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, the amount is held for release by a reviewer, and either party may appeal within 30 days."
